Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='secretaryreviews', at=datetime(2026, 10, 24, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title='The secretary reviews the triage cards: it withdraws duplicates and noise with a why and never performs one', body='*The secretary reviews the triage cards* (§10.6). Two verbs, `triage_cards` and `triage_withdraw`; the rule is `SECRETARY.md`\'s "Reviewing the agent\'s cards": withdraw duplicates and noise with a REQUIRED `why`, leave the rest for the owner, and never perform one (it holds no tap). A hold is DERIVED from what is still open; every withdrawal and hold writes a `Reviewed` line. `scripts/hourly-triage.sh` runs `suzatary secretary review` at the end of each pass, before `safe-push.sh`; it exits zero when cards are left and when the model is unreachable. A pass with no new mail runs no model and still calls `safe-push.sh`, so what the server wrote since the last pass (taps, proposals, conversations, the app\'s chain writes) is committed within five minutes. `suzatary secretary reviews --since <date>` is the day\'s decisions for the briefing. The old mechanism remains for objects `triage` wrote to the chain before batches (two open todos, 2026-09-10); `untrusted = []` waits until those are settled by hand.', rationale='Shipped in 2.1.17, 2026-10-24 (ARCHITECTURE §10.6). The two todos triage wrote before batches date from 2026-09-10.', supersedes=()))